            <ArticleTitle>Stenting the sigmoid colon in a terminally ill patient with prostate cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>153-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Large bowel obstruction in the terminally ill patient can be difficult to manage. We describe a patient with sigmoid colon obstruction caused by metastatic prostate cancer in the pelvis who required hospitalization because of severe pain and obstructive symptoms. Treatment with an endoscopically placed self-expandable metal stent allowed the patient to have immediate resolution of symptoms and to receive hospice care at home.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
